    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Document any changes with notes and, if necessary, additional photos.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Following the visual audit, the odometer is verified against the Load Receipt (LR) bilty. The bilty lists the original mileage at pickup and the expected mileage at delivery, allowing the verifier to confirm that the recorded distance matches the vehicle’s current reading.</p>
<p>This step prevents mileage manipulation and ensures compliance with regulatory requirements. Any discrepancy between the bilty and the odometer must be explained and approved by both parties before the handover is finalized.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Read the odometer on the motorcycle’s dashboard.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Cross‑check the figure with the LR bilty mileage column.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Record the verification result in the handover sheet.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>The final stage of the handover is the signed condition sign‑off. Both the carrier’s representative and the consignee sign the handover sheet, confirming that the vehicle has been inspected, the odometer verified, and that the condition is satisfactory.</p>
<p>This signed document serves as a legal record of the handover and protects against future disputes. The carrier retains a copy for its records, while the consignee retains theirs for reference during the warranty or return period.</p>

<p>By adhering to these steps—daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed sign‑off—companies ensure transparency, maintain vehicle integrity, and uphold customer trust throughout the delivery process.</p></div>
